npc.Raider_Trork_Warlord.name = Trork warlord
npc.Kweebec_Defender.name = Razorleaf guard
npc.Kweebec_Chief.name = Kweebec chief
items.Nakasar_Peuples_Trophy_Trork.name = Trork trophy
items.Nakasar_Peuples_Trophy_Trork.description = Skulls taken from the raiders of a repelled raid. Display them proudly at home.
items.Nakasar_Peuples_Echo_Seed.name = Echo Seed
items.Nakasar_Peuples_Echo_Seed.description = Given by the Kweebec chief to the champion of their people. They say it still sings with the Grandfather's voice, and could draw water where nothing grows.
command.raid.desc = Expected or running raid at the nearest village, and the last raid's report
command.raidStart.desc = Starts a raid on the nearest village right now (daytime too)
command.raidFinish.desc = Ends the running raid: won or lost
command.raidFinish.arg = gagne (won) or perdu (lost)
command.raidCancel.desc = Cancels the running or expected raid at the nearest village
command.raidSchedule.desc = Schedules a raid tonight at the nearest village
command.chain.desc = Your progress in the quest chain of the nearest village's people
command.chainStep.desc = Sets the number of chain steps done (0 to 5)
command.chainStep.arg = steps done (0 to 5)
dialogue.job.raid = Any news of the Trorks?
dialogue.Kweebec_Guard.auxArmes = To arms! They're here! Hold the line with us!
dialogue.Kweebec_Guard.rumeur = The Trorks lit a fire to the east. Tonight smells of axes.
dialogue.Kweebec_Watcher.auxArmes = To arms! I can see them from the tower, there are many!
dialogue.Kweebec_Watcher.rumeur = I saw smoke behind the hills. A Trork camp, surely.
# ---- Step 6: Kweebec chain ----
chain.stepDone = Chain step done: "{title}". Go back to the village chief.
chain.status = {people} chain: {done}/5 steps. Next: {next}
chain.set = Chain steps done: {done}.
chain.Kweebec.step1 = heal the young sprouts (10 Sap, Tolerated rank)
chain.Kweebec.step2 = free the prisoners from the Trork camp (Friend rank)
chain.Kweebec.step3 = replant the burned grove (Friend rank)
chain.Kweebec.step4 = watch over the Grandfather during a night raid (Host rank)
chain.Kweebec.step5 = receive the Echo Seed (Champion rank)
dialogue.hint.chain = starts the people's chain step
dialogue.hint.chainSap = gives 10 Sap to the chief
dialogue.hint.chainSeed = receives the Echo Seed
dialogue.fail.rank.Champion = you must be a Champion of the Kweebecs
request.plant.found = The grove is in ashes. Plant {item} there (oak seeds will do).
request.Kweebec_Chain_Prisoners.title = Free the prisoners from the Trork camp
request.Kweebec_Chain_Prisoners.task = Bring the prisoner back to the village. The camp is {distance} blocks away, {direction}.
request.Kweebec_Chain_Grove.title = Replant the burned grove
request.Kweebec_Chain_Grove.task = Sprouts planted: {count}/{needed}. The grove is {distance} blocks away, {direction}.
request.Kweebec_Chain_Vigil.title = Watch over the Grandfather
request.Kweebec_Chain_Vigil.task = Repel tonight's raid on the village. The village heart is {distance} blocks away, {direction}.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.npc = Rootsinger
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.role = Village chief
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.aurevoir = May the sap keep you.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.nouvelles = And the Trorks?
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.nouvellesTexte = The wind carries their drums. Keep your eyes open, and your ears too.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.accepter = I'll see to it.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.accepte = Go, and come back whole. The Grandfather is waiting.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.auxArmes = No time for songs! The Trorks are in the grove: defend the Grandfather!
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.honni = Go away. The Grandfather wants none of you here.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.etranger = The Grandfather is fading, stranger. I will not trust his sap to you.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.commentAider = How do I earn your trust?
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.conseil = Help the village: the board's requests. Once we tolerate you, come back to me.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.voirDemandes = See the requests
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.seve = The Grandfather is fading: the Trorks steal his sap and the young sprouts wither. Bring us sap, and we will see if you are a friend.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.donnerSeve = Here are ten drops of sap.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.failSeve = you must be Tolerated by the Kweebecs and carry 10 Sap
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.prisonniers = The sprouts are greening again, thank you. But the Trorks hold one of ours in their camp. When you are our friend, bring them back.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.prisonniersEnCours = The prisoner is waiting somewhere in the Trork camp. Bring them to the village heart.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.bosquet = You brought them back! The little one still sings. The Trorks burned the grove where they played: replant it, six oak sprouts.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.bosquetEnCours = The grove is waiting for its sprouts. Six, no fewer: the Grandfather will count them.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.veille = The grove grows back. The Trorks saw it, they will come. When you are our host, watch over the Grandfather with us during their raid.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.veilleAcceptee = They will come tonight. Stay near the Grandfather, with our guards.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.veilleEnCours = Tonight the Trorks will come. Stay near the Grandfather, with our guards.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.graine = You held through the night. The Grandfather sang me a seed for you: an Echo Seed. I will give it only to the champion of our people.
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.recevoirGraine = Receive the Echo Seed
dialogue.Kweebec_Chef.fin = The Echo Seed sings in your pocket. The Feran, they say, will recognise it.
